{"kind":"request","text":"Proof-reuse semantic boundary found during read-only preparation for 7c0, while 121a remains under checker review. No implementation or project check ran.\n\nI propose one command-local multi-root room verifier, with a shared set of actually proven prefixes and content, cumulative work ceilings, one final union coverage/trust record, and final per-scope summaries. Every requested room scope is a root at depth0; foreign depth is the least distance from roots actually followed. Existing standalone verify(source, options) keeps its single-target semantics and all existing tests unchanged. No discovery-only data becomes proof. Cached proofs bind the exact source, incarnation, entry hash and semantic/code/trust options. Expected heads, causal-prefix checks, contradiction invalidation and failed-fold quarantine remain required. This appears to implement wanted1 directly rather than re-proving a Membership prefix for each target.\n\nThe choice matters because the current contract section9.4 defines depth from one target, while current #prove already accepts a previously proven fact before its depth guard. A new batch API/room report has no stated root-set rule. Concrete small example: S can prove U at depth1. A fresh isolated T, which needs S and then U at depth2, is incomplete with depth1. If S was already successfully proved as another root of the same room command, T can use that checked proof as a lemma. A shared room proof can then be complete, with S/U included in its union coverage, even though isolated T would have stopped for work. This is a different resource-boundary outcome; no unproved fact is being accepted.\n\nDetached text has the same question. Current #settle may discharge a missing text when the run has already decoded matching content from another checked source; the content can also alter historical byte recovery. Sharing actual room-run knowledge is natural for one multi-root proof, but preserving fresh single-target traversal/coverage for every target would require target-local conditional proof/text/settlement certificates. Merely resetting Run.depth or caching a boolean hash is unsound under that stricter interpretation. A fallback that re-verifies every text-sensitive target could also violate wanted1 by proving Membership again, so I will not adopt a narrower text-independent-only cache as the delivered scope.\n\nPlease adopt the proposed multi-root room-proof semantics (with a precise contract/readme clarification and one union coverage/trust description), or require strict per-target fresh-traversal equivalence with full conditional certificates. Either choice keeps all defaults, standalone results, real HTTP accounting and the accepted prior-head control unchanged. The new 2,000-member run must still report every actual scope consistent. Order remains 121a, then7c0, thenJ4; current121a work continues independently.","body":{"conditions":"Dispose the room proof's root/depth/text-evidence semantics before implementation: shared multi-root verification with union coverage, or strict fresh-target traversal equivalence. Preserve standalone behavior, actual derivation, defaults, and full Membership proof reuse.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}